SUMMARY:DuPont/Corn Mill Shoals\; a Saunter 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**We are the Sloth Hiking Group: “We will
  get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike g
 roups don’t !!**\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4**\nI am 
 going to unravel my stress at Corn Mill Shoals in DuPont Forest.\nUp to 12
  ppl (only) are welcome to join me.\nI will spend (up to) 2 hours at the f
 alls swimming\, eating\, reading and pretending to meditate.\n**Hike Detai
 ls:**\nLength: 2.5 mi RT (in & out)\; Accum Ascent: 250 ft (all on the ret
 urn)\nPace: 1.5mph – because I’m an ol’ Codger.\nDescription: Easy. 
 Old roadbed\;\n**Optional: Swimming & wading.**\nDrive time: 25 min\; 17 m
 i 1-way\n**Alternate meeting place:**\n**Google Map = “Corn Mill Shoals 
 Access”: 10:00AM**\nApprx return time: 2:00 pm\nCarpool contributions ap
 preciated. $3.00 suggested\nTHIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE. This event is 
 NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Do
 gs (and Masters) required to be ‘on-leash' in DuPont. Small (lap)dogs ma
 y carpool. Large dogs will drive themselves.\nWeather Check: Cedar Mountai
 n\, NC\nWeather cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE
  WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\n(I currently have 3.5 driver(s). (=12p
 pl)\nWe suggest masks and open windows while carpooling. Only you know you
 r own health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your hea
 lth or the health of others. Please bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid 
 bringing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nI
 ncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair. Obstreperous ra
 ucous yawping is discouraged.\n**Description**\;\nCome prepared to meditat
 e\, practice your Tai-Chi\, **森林浴**\, read a book\, prepare a meal\,
  play a flute\, play in the water.\n**UnRuffle/UnRavel:** To experience a 
 time of quiet in a manner that you feel worthwhile. Démêlez votre stress
 .\nEngage the 5 senses (sight\, smell\, touch\, taste\, hearing)\,\nObserv
 e the movement of the forest & water.\nBreathe the aroma of the air\, wate
 r\, plants and forest.\nFeel the texture of the air\, water\, trees and pl
 ants.\nListening to the sound of air\, water\, critters & birds\;\nTaste t
 he air of the breezes or soothing snacks.\nAll hikes are at your own risk.
  You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: 
 There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant
 \, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability t
 he leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members
  for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur 
 while participating in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle dur
 ing this trip. **Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules and
  regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\,
  and not to become intentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s)
  also has the right to use any images collected on this trip for recording
  on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: curmudgeonhiker@gmail.co
 m\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\nPics: https://www
 .flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums
