SUMMARY:UnRuffle yo’self at Potholes Falls
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**We are the Sloth Hiking Group: “We will
  get there when we get there.”**\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H
 4EK2vt4**\nI am going to unravel my stress at Pothole Falls (& beach) @ Bu
 llpen Rd Bridge south of Highlands\, NC. If you value more than a moment o
 f silent\, meditative calm\; Up to 12 ppl are welcome to join me.\n**Socia
 l ‘hour’ at 9 am. Cattle Call at 9:15a)**\n**Description**\;\nPothole 
 Falls is a unique pothole formation cascade. **There is also a ‘beach ar
 ea’ a ¼ mile upstream.** We will spend (up to) 2 hrs at the Cascades. C
 ome prepared to swim\, meditate\, practice your Tai-Chi\, \, **森林浴**
 \, read a book\, prepare a meal\, play a flute. This is a popular spot\; w
 e will be sharing with others.\nThis is a time to UnRavel – leave your s
 tresses and concerns back home.\n**Hike Details:**\nLength: 0.25 mi\; 50 f
 t descent\nDifficulty: Short steep trail\; some steps.\nDrive time: 1.25hr
 s/42 mi (1-way) High clearance vehicle reqr’d.\nGoogle Map: “Pothole F
 alls\; old iron bridge\, Bull Pen Road\, Cashiers\, NC”\nApprx return ti
 me: 3 PM\nCarpool contributions appreciated. $4.00 suggested\nWeather Chec
 k: Cashiers\, NC\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\n(I 
 currently have 1 driver(s).\nWe suggest slightly open windows while carpoo
 ling. Only you know your own health status so judge accordingly if an even
 t may endanger your health or the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra
  pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at
  the end of the hike.\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is N
 OT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs.\nWe
 ll trained dogs (you don’t have to yell.) can be 'off-leash'. 'On leash'
  during the lunch stop. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive
  themselves.\n***UnRavel:*** To experience a time of quiet in a manner tha
 t you feel worthwhile.\nEngage the 5 senses (sight\, smell\, touch\, taste
 \, hearing)\,\nObserve the movement of the forest & water.\nBreathe the ar
 oma of the air\, water\, plants and forest.\nFeel the texture of the air\,
  water\, trees and plants.\nListening to the sound of air\, water\, critte
 rs & birds\;\nTaste the air of the breezes or soothing snacks.\nAll hikes 
 are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate
  equipment.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is a volunteer and not 
 a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize th
 is event. There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each p
 articipant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release from l
 iability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, a
 nd members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which mi
 ght occur while participating in this activity or while traveling in any v
 ehicle during this trip. Each participant further agrees to abide by the r
 ules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the lea
 der(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from the group. The lea
 der(s) also has the right to use any images collected on this trip for rec
 ording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: curmudgeonhiker@gm
 ail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)
