SUMMARY:the Park at Flat Rock\; A Walk 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A WALK IN THE PARK**\nWe will Tour de Par
 ks of the area. One at a time. You are welcome to join us.\nThis Week: The
  Park at Flat Rock.\nWe are the Sloth Walking Team: “We will get there w
 hen we get there.”\n**Up to 12 ppl** are welcome to join us.\n**https://
 www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bsh_8qxUfDY**\n**Description:** the 66-acre park h
 as a flat\, open green space and a 1.3 mile trail (shortcuts available) th
 at you can walk or run.\nhttps://flatrockparkfoundation.org/the-park/\nLen
 gth: <1.5 mi\; Total ascent: 25 ft\nDifficulty: Easy\, peasy\nSuitable for
  beginners? Yes\nApprx return time: 11:30pm\n**Optional:** Lunch @ TBD.\nW
 eather Check: Hendersonville\, NC\nWeather cancellations will be posted at
  6:30am.\n**This is a dog-participant walk.** This event is NOT for those 
 who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Dogs are welcome
  (IF their masters are well trained). 'On leash' rules apply.\nDue to rece
 nt events\, Bigfoot discussions are no longer permitted.\nhttps://flatrock
 parkfoundation.org/the-park/\nAll walks are at your own risk. You are resp
 onsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer
  of this event is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function o
 f the organizer is only to organize this event. There are certain risks in
 herent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend
  this event\, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun F
 riends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury
 \, illness\, or personal loss which might occur while participating in thi
 s activity or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. Each partic
 ipant further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safe
 ty\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intention
 ally separated from the group. The leader(s) also has the right to use any
  images collected on this trip for recording on website photo collections.
 \ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 8
 28.393.0297 (text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N
 05/albums**
